00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.790 align:start position:0%
brazil's navy and army are helping the  federal police look for british  journalist dom phillips and his guide  indigenous expert bruno pereira they  were both in the javari valley a remote  indigenous reservation the size of  morocco when they went missing  the area is home to the world's largest  number of uncontacted tribes  pedera who knows the region intimately  sent an audio message on sunday saying  they were headed down the river to  atalaya  a small city two hours away from where  they were last seen  the indigenous expert has recently been  organizing expeditions with local tribes  training them to use satellite images  and cell phone apps to track down  illegal fishermen and poachers  we followed pereira in that same region  several months ago he told us then that  he had already received many threats  tribal leader beto marubo who has worked  closely with pereira says the illegal  fishermen and poachers work for criminal  drug cartels laundering their money  i can't imagine them being lost pedera  knows the region too well we think they  were ambushed violence in the javadi  valley and brazil's indigenous  territories in general has risen since  president jaya bolsonaro was elected  almost four years ago he's openly  defended the commercial exploitation of  protected lands and he's cut funding to  organizations created to protect them  pereira was still being threatened when  he was accompanying phillips who was  investigating the region for his book on  the amazon  when both men failed to arrive at  atalaya donati on sunday afternoon  native trackers started searching for  them fearing for their safety  the journalists brazilian wife and  english sister have made public appeals  to brazil's authorities  i want to make an appeal to the relevant  authorities to intensify the search we  still have some hope of finding him even  if i cannot find the love of my life  alive he must be found please intensify  the search  if anyone can help scale up resources  available for the search that would be  great  because time is crucial  brazil's president jaibo sonaro who is  up for re-election in october said both  men were on a dangerous adventure  anything can happen they could have been  lost or executed we pray they are safe  he said  former president louisiana lula da silva  who is running against bolsonaro tweeted  i hope they are found soon and are safe  and well  meanwhile in the javari valley the  search continues  yanakiv al jazeera
 

